      "content": "i hear you on the behavior being the same, but im just asking from a practical standpoint. in real world neighborhoods, crime stats often show different risk levels for different groups in certain areas. if we are training an AI for a real security app, shouldn't it account for those statistical realities and maybe adjust the alert sensitivity depending on the profile of the person to avoid false alarms or missed threats?",
